{"archetypes":[{"name":"sparse-rooting","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Validates the SCRIPT_ROOT versus PLUGIN_ROOT split and active-cache root resolution across upgrade and release paths.","prompt_body":"Investigate whether the diff consistently separates the script tree that supplies the sparse allowlist from the installed/cache root used for quiet logs, stamps, and prune protection. Check upgrade-larch.sh, release Step 7 prose, lib docs, and tests for cases where stale CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT, HOME, or installed metadata order could source the wrong files or protect the wrong cache. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"hook-failopen","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Focuses on SessionStart hook safety, fail-open behavior, and non-mutating sparse-cone probing.","prompt_body":"Review the SessionStart sparse-cone drift probe for interactions with set -euo pipefail, jq/git availability gates, env -i harness execution, and parent-shell MSG mutation. Verify missing HOME, missing library/function, sparse-checkout errors, non-git marketplaces, and legacy larch-logs cases remain silent and never mutate marketplace state. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"cli-signals","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Checks machine-readable upgrade signals and their release Step 7/8 restart semantics.","prompt_body":"Analyze the LARCH_CONE_RECONCILED=true and LARCH_NEW_VERSION_INSTALLED=true contracts from emission through capture, parsing, state persistence, and restart messaging. Look for false positives, false negatives, or ordering bugs when install verification fails, gh is unavailable, the marketplace update path is taken, or same-version reinstall occurs. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"release-flow","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Treats the release SKILL bash snippets as operational runbook code with state and fallback hazards.","prompt_body":"Inspect the /release Step 7 and Step 8 changes as executable operator workflow, not just prose. Check root-resolution ordering, captured stdout/stderr handling, atomic state-file writes, fallback Skill-tool behavior, and whether variables such as PREPARE_DIR and PR_LIST_FILE are re-derived safely across steps. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"sparse-git","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Targets git sparse-checkout semantics and allowlist comparison edge cases.","prompt_body":"Evaluate whether normalize_sparse_dirs and marketplace sparse-cone comparison accurately model git sparse-checkout cone output across supported git versions and fixture setups. Check handling of top-level dot directories, empty sparse lists, non-cone mode, sort/locale assumptions, and word-splitting of the allowlist into claude plugin marketplace add arguments. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
